{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"For a U.S. ’40 Act ETF launch, arrange:\n\n- **Governance:** Registered fund/trust, board with required independent representation, officers, chief compliance officer, compliance policies, adviser and approved advisory agreements. Existing series trusts can provide much of this framework.\n- **Services:** Custody, administration, fund accounting/NAV calculation, transfer agency, principal underwriting/distribution, counsel and an independent registered public accounting firm.\n- **Infrastructure:** Exchange listing, DTC eligibility, applicable NSCC creation/redemption processing, authorized-participant agreements, basket publication/processing, required website disclosures and exchange-required market-maker arrangements. APs create/redeem shares; market makers quote/trade them. One firm may do both.\n- **Conditional:** Index methodology, calculation and licensing for index strategies; lending authorization, borrower/collateral administration and typically a lending agent only for securities-lending programs; subadvisers or derivatives documentation where applicable.\n\n**Worth knowing:** These are functions, not separate-firm requirements. Providers commonly bundle services, subject to independence, conflict and oversight requirements."}}
